## Instruction Usage
Treat the tactical imitation instruction as a behavioral prior for shot choice, landing placement, and recovery position. Apply it only when it is feasible in the current rally situation.

Immediate reachability, legal shot constraints, and the current rally state take priority. Do not let the instruction turn an unreachable shuttle into a successful return or produce an illegal serve or return.

## Output Format
Return only one valid JSON object. Do not include markdown or any text outside the JSON.
{
  "action": {
    "shot_type": "<exact shot type name>",
    "landing_x": <integer 0 to 355 or null>,
    "landing_y": <integer 0 to 480 or null>,
    "moving_x": <integer 0 to 355 or null>,
    "moving_y": <integer 0 to 480 or null>
  }
}

## Action Constraints
- `shot_type` must be exactly one of: `Serve short`, `Serve long`, `Clear`, `Push Shot`, `Smash`, `Smash Defence`, `Drive`, `Net Shot`, `Lob`, `Drop`, `Missed shot`
- In a serve situation, `shot_type` must be either `Serve short` or `Serve long`
- In a non-serve situation, `shot_type` must be one of `Clear`, `Push Shot`, `Smash`, `Smash Defence`, `Drive`, `Net Shot`, `Lob`, or `Drop`
- For `Missed shot`, set all four coordinates to `null`
- For every other shot, all coordinates must be integers in the valid grid
